   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p>Greetings,<div><br></div><div>I have been wanting to mimic a plot from ggplot in ggvis to make use of interaction capabilities of ggvis. But I am facing a problem with layer_paths while using <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">stroke=~</font></div><div><div><br></div></div><div>This is the code I tried to use </div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(ggplot2)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(ggvis)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">time = c(1,4,5,10,15, 17)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">action = c(&#39;action1&#39;, &#39;action2&#39;, &#39;action1&#39;, &#39;action2&#39;, &#39;action3&#39;, &#39;action4&#39;)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">dataf = data.frame(time, action)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">ggplot(dataf, aes(time, y=1)) + <b>geom_path(aes(group=1, color=action), size=2)</b> + geom_point(aes(col=action), size=8)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">dataf %&gt;% ggvis(x=~time, y:=1) %&gt;% <b>layer_paths(stroke=~action, strokeWidth:=2)</b> %&gt;% layer_points(fill=~action, size:=150)</font></div></div></div><div><br></div><div>But ggvis behavior of layer_paths is quite different from ggplots behavior from geom_paths regarding line coloring. As you can see from the following two graphs, ggplot changes color lines as expected with geom_paths, but layer_paths stick with the first color only.</div><div><br></div><div>Is this intended? Am I missing something? <br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-TOXjNgVm9bc/VJLdACKossI/AAAAAAAAAVk/tA2IEbCu87s/s1600/ggplot_diff_color.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-TOXjNgVm9bc/VJLdACKossI/AAAAAAAAAVk/tA2IEbCu87s/s1600/ggplot_diff_color.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484808376000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Gn6dIeSC0jUwB5tIgeBWL\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-TOXjNgVm9bc/VJLdACKossI/AAAAAAAAAVk/tA2IEbCu87s/s400/ggplot_diff_color.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"181\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-ZnVFi1LvizM/VJLerRIh0oI/AAAAAAAAAV0/mrqY40X_ftU/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2014-12-18%2Bat%2B4.02.04%2BPM.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-ZnVFi1LvizM/VJLerRIh0oI/AAAAAAAAAV0/mrqY40X_ftU/s1600/Screen%252BShot%252B2014-12-18%252Bat%252B4.02.04%252BPM.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484808376000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0eRSoOk4G0cKvVLwvlCQYd\"><img src=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-ZnVFi1LvizM/VJLerRIh0oI/AAAAAAAAAV0/mrqY40X_ftU/s400/Screen%2BShot%2B2014-12-18%2Bat%2B4.02.04%2BPM.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"237\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
